## Edit C or C++ here

The complete user-owned source root is:

```text
android/src/main/cpp/
```

`math.cpp`, `text.cpp`, `helpers.c`, and `helpers.h` are live starter code.
Place an export marker immediately before a top-level C++ definition:

```cpp
// @SupernoteExport
double add(double left, double right) {
  return left + right;
}
```

Call the default export from the parent plugin:

```typescript
import $MODULE_NAME_RAW from '$NPM_NAME_RAW';

const total = await $MODULE_NAME_RAW.add(20, 22);
```

Supported boundary types are exactly `bool`, `double`, and UTF-8
`std::string` by value, plus `void` returns. C files compile as C23 and may
provide helpers but cannot export. C++/generated bindings compile as C++23.
Do not write JNI registration/loaders or edit generated CMake.

## Ownership and lifecycle warning

Update preserves the complete `android/src/main/cpp/` tree and replaces
generator infrastructure, including metadata, package/wrapper/declaration
files, this README, Gradle/CMake, generated Kotlin/C++, loading, registration,
and autolinking.

Update has no dry-run or file-level diff. **Remove deletes the entire module,
including the C/C++ tree. Commit first.**

## Build and continue

From the parent plugin root, run `./buildPlugin.sh` on macOS/Linux or
`.\buildPlugin.ps1` in Windows PowerShell. The parent build regenerates bindings
and writes `build/outputs/plugin.snplg` for the official default; if the
parent's `PluginConfig.json` name differs, use the actual output name.

